ng contact at 0. The minimizer premise here belongs to the ordinary manuscript model; formal-interface hypotheses remain on the separate Lean target. This classification does not prove a transport between formal models.","citation_ids":["support_contact_source","support_contact_lean_source","support_diffusion_source"],"evidence_ids":["support_source_bindings_20261024","support_graph_semantic_review_pending"],"id":"support.contact_derivatives","kind":"claim","label":"Endpoint contact and slope bounds, including zero","locator":"variation.tex:119–127; contact-derivatives","source_id":"support_tex_variation","statement":"For an admissible minimizer gamma and G,S,q as in support.contact, G'(s)=s-q(s) and G''(s)=1-q'(s) on compact strips. At every s in S intersect (0,1), q(s)=s and q'(s)<=1. If 0 is in S, then q(0)=0 and G(h)=(1/2)(1-q'(0))h^2+o(h^2), so the right derivative q'(0)<=1.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/support.contact_derivatives","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/support.contact_derivatives","id":"field:c3dede06ca5d3e3544410e2bb399666931a7cb6e540a70336738dae73428f780","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/support.contact_derivatives","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/support.contact_derivatives","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22support.contact_derivatives%22%2C%22support.contact%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df1129